COMMENT ON COLUMN ltc_dp_collapsed.chronometric_age."chronometricAgeUncertaintyInYears" IS 'The temporal uncertainty of the earliestChronometricAge and latestChronometicAge in years. [http://rs.tdwg.org/chrono/terms/chronometricAgeUncertaintyInYears]';
COMMENT ON COLUMN ltc_dp_collapsed.chronometric_age."earliestChronometricAge" IS 'The maximum/earliest/oldest possible age of a specimen as determined by a dating method. [http://rs.tdwg.org/chrono/terms/earliestChronometricAge]';
COMMENT ON COLUMN ltc_dp_collapsed.chronometric_age."earliestChronometricAgeReferenceSystem" IS 'The reference system associated with the earliestChronometricAge. [http://rs.tdwg.org/chrono/terms/earliestChronometricAgeReferenceSystem]';
COMMENT ON COLUMN ltc_dp_collapsed.chronometric_age."latestChronometricAge" IS 'The minimum/latest/youngest possible age of a specimen as determined by a dating method. [http://rs.tdwg.org/chrono/terms/latestChronometricAge]';
COMMENT ON COLUMN ltc_dp_collapsed.chronometric_age."latestChronometricAgeReferenceSystem" IS 'The reference system associated with the latestChronometricAge. [http://rs.tdwg.org/chrono/terms/latestChronometricAgeReferenceSystem]';
COMMENT ON COLUMN ltc_dp_collapsed.chronometric_age."verbatimChronometricAge" IS 'The verbatim age for a specimen, whether reported by a dating assay, associated references, or legacy information. [http://rs.tdwg.org/chrono/terms/verbatimChronometricAge]';

